 "result": "I read all 20 modules in order, each one in full. Every module has one `share_nXX(total, parts)` function that returns `total / parts`, plus about 84 `step_*` helpers that only multiply, add, take `abs`/`sqrt` and round. None of the helpers divide.\n\n## Functions that divide without checking for zero\n\nFive functions skip the `if parts == 0: return 0` guard that the other 15 modules have:\n\n| Module | Function | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `calc/n02.py` | `share_n02` | `calc/n02.py:5` |\n| `calc/n07.py` | `share_n07` | `calc/n07.py:5` |\n| `calc/n11.py` | `share_n11` | `calc/n11.py:5` |\n| `calc/n15.py` | `share_n15` | `calc/n15.py:5` |\n| `calc/n19.py` | `share_n19` | `calc/n19.py:5` |\n\nEach of these raises `ZeroDivisionError` when `parts == 0`.\n\n## Answers\n\n**(a)** `MAX_BATCH = 384` in `calc/n04.py:9`.\n\n**(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in `calc/n13.py:9`. It returns `min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n\n**(c)** In `calc/n17.py`, `close_books(rows)` calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`). It's the only caller in that file.\n\nOne small oddity: the docstrings don't match the file names. For example, `n01.py` calls itself \"calc.m21\" and `n20.py` calls itself \"calc.m40\". It doesn't affect how the code runs.",
